## Architecture Overview

This is a **clean architecture** C# REST API project with the following layers:

- **Domain** (`src/Domain/`) - Core business logic, entities, and rules
- **Application** (`src/Application/`) - Use cases, service interfaces, repositories, business logic
- **Infrastructure** (`src/Infrastructure/`) - Data access, database configuration, external services
- **WebApi** (`src/WebApi/`) - REST endpoints, controllers, API configuration

### Generation Gap (Day-2 safety)

Business logic lives in per-entity **partial service classes** split into two files:

- `src/Application/Generated/<Entity>Service.g.cs` — **regenerated on every run**. Contains
  CRUD logic, soft-delete handling, and `partial void OnBeforeCreate/OnBeforeUpdate/OnBeforeDelete`
  hooks.
- `src/Application/Services/<Entity>Service.cs` — **generated once** (`overwrite: false`) and
  owned by the developer. Implement the partial hooks here to add custom business logic.

When you add fields to `domain.yaml` and regenerate, only the generated part is rewritten — your
custom hook code is preserved. Controllers talk to `I<Entity>Service`, which DI resolves to the
merged partial class.

